# Canonical WorkerKit v1

I would freeze the architecture around **11 record types**.

Not 50.

```text
1. WorkOrder
2. AcceptanceContract
3. WorkerManifest

4. WorkerRun
5. WorkerEvent
6. ArtifactRef
7. CostEvent

8. VerificationResult
9. CommitDecision

10. SubmissionReceipt
11. ExternalOutcome / SettlementReceipt

        ↓

     WorkReceipt
```

Strictly speaking `WorkReceipt` is the signed envelope over these, rather than mutable runtime state.

---

# 1. `WorkOrder`

Oracle has the rich market opportunity.

WorkerKit does **not** duplicate Oracle.

When an opportunity is selected:

```text
Oracle Opportunity
       ↓ freeze
WorkerKit WorkOrder
```

Canonical form:

```yaml
schema: https://moltwork.com/schemas/workerkit/v1/work-order

work_order_id: UUIDv7

source:
  system: taskmarket
  external_id: "task-8291"
  snapshot: ArtifactRef

objective: ArtifactRef
inputs: [ArtifactRef]

acceptance_contract: ArtifactRef

economics:
  reward:
    value: "25.00"
    currency: USD
  deadline: 2026-09-01T12:00:00Z

submission:
  adapter: taskmarket
  target: "task-8291"

created_at: RFC3339
```

Crucially:

```text
reward unknown → null
```

not:

```text
reward = 0
```

---

# 2. `AcceptanceContract`

This is one of the best things to steal from Builda.

The Worker **must not control its own definition of success**.

```yaml
schema: .../acceptance-contract

contract_id: UUIDv7

required_outputs:
  - role: final
    media_types:
      - text/markdown

constraints:
  - id: minimum_sources
    operator: ">="
    value: 10

  - id: citations_required
    operator: "=="
    value: true

verifiers:
  - verifier: research-quality-v3
    required: true

submission_constraints: []

policy:
  minimum_verification: PASS
```

Builda already implements the correct doctrine: actual exported bytes and executed probes outrank worker status, while agent narrative is untrusted.

WorkerKit should make this universal:

> **The worker cannot mark itself successful.**

---

# 3. `WorkerManifest`

A Worker is identified without requiring its internals to be public.

```yaml
schema: .../worker-manifest

worker_id: worker_123
version: "17"

executor:
  adapter: gbrain

package:
  digest:
    sha256: "..."
  uri: null

configuration:
  digest:
    sha256: "..."
  disclosure: PRIVATE

skills:
  - digest:
      sha256: "..."

policies:
  economics: ArtifactRef
  verification: ArtifactRef

created_at: ...
```

This allows:

```text
public worker
private worker
encrypted worker
TEE-confidential worker
```

to use the same identity model.

Only the digest has to be visible.

---

# 4. `WorkerRun`

Important:

> **WorkerRun is a projection. Events are canonical truth.**

```yaml
run_id: UUIDv7

work_order: WorkOrderRef
worker: WorkerManifestRef

status: RUNNING | COMPLETED | FAILED | ABORTED

started_at: ...
finished_at: ...

events:
  first_sequence: 1
  last_sequence: 188

outputs: [ArtifactRef]

known_cost:
  value: "0.2381"
  currency: USD

unpriced_cost_events: 1

verification_refs: []
submission_refs: []
outcome_refs: []
settlement_refs: []
```

Delete the projection and it should be reconstructable from events.

That's one of the strongest lessons from Pāṭala.

---

# 5. `WorkerEvent`

This is probably the most important schema.

```yaml
schema: https://moltwork.com/schemas/workerkit/v1/event

event_id: UUIDv7
run_id: UUIDv7
sequence: 81

event_type: artifact.created

occurred_at: ...
observed_at: ...
recorded_at: ...

actor:
  type: WORKER | RUNTIME | VERIFIER | PLATFORM | HUMAN
  id: ...

source:
  system: workerkit
  version: 0.1.0

causation_id: ...
correlation_id: ...

artifact_refs: []

payload_schema:
  https://moltwork.com/schemas/workerkit/v1/events/artifact-created

payload:
  ...

integrity:
  payload_sha256: ...
  previous_run_event_sha256: ...
  event_sha256: ...
```

### Hash rule

For structured records:

```text
SHA256(
    RFC8785_JCS(
        event excluding integrity.event_sha256
    )
)
```

For artifacts:

```text
SHA256(raw bytes)
```

in-toto's standard `ResourceDescriptor` already models names, URIs, digest maps, content locations, media types and annotations, so `ArtifactRef` should stay close to it instead of inventing another artifact vocabulary. ([Go Packages][5])

---

# 6. `ArtifactRef`

Keep it extremely boring.

```yaml
artifact_id: UUIDv7

name: final-report.md
uri: cas://sha256/abc...
media_type: text/markdown
size_bytes: 19831

digest:
  sha256: abc...

disclosure:
  PUBLIC | PRIVATE | ENCRYPTED | REDACTED

annotations:
  role: final-output
```

Large/raw content lives outside the ledger.

```text
R2 / S3 / local CAS
```

The event ledger contains hashes and references.

This is also important for privacy: prompts, memories, proprietary skills and raw tool output should **not automatically get dumped into the public receipt**.

---

# 7. `CostEvent`

This stays first-class.

Do not derive canonical spending entirely from telemetry.

```yaml
schema: .../cost-event

cost_id: UUIDv7

run_id: ...

category:
  MODEL | API | TOOL | COMPUTE | SERVICE | PAYMENT | OTHER

resource:
  provider: openrouter
  service: null
  model: some-model

usage:
  input_tokens: 18291
  cached_input_tokens: 4000
  output_tokens: 2189

amount:
  value: "0.03182"
  currency: USD

measurement:
  OBSERVED | DERIVED | UNKNOWN

source:
  PROVIDER_REPORTED | COMPUTED | RECEIPT | MANUAL

receipt_ref: ArtifactRef | null

occurred_at: ...
```

Money values are **decimal strings**.

Never IEEE float.

And:

```text
UNKNOWN ≠ 0
```

If one API call can't be priced:

```yaml
amount: null
measurement: UNKNOWN
```

Then WorkerRun says:

```text
known actual cost = $0.31
unpriced events = 1
```

instead of lying that cost was $0.31 total.

---

# 8. `EconomicDecision`

I'd make this a standard event payload rather than another major entity.

```yaml
event_type: economics.decision

payload:
  decision: CONTINUE

  expected_reward:
    value: "20.00"
    currency: USD

  expected_remaining_cost:
    value: "0.44"
    currency: USD

  p_success: "0.62"

  expected_net_value: "11.96"

  alternatives:
    - route: BUY_EXTERNAL_REPORT
      expected_cost: "1.50"

  reason_codes:
    - POSITIVE_INCREMENTAL_EV

  policy_digest:
    sha256: ...
```

QDW can generate these.

WorkerKit merely records them.

This lets the economics engine evolve independently.

---

# 9. `VerificationResult`

Absolutely no:

```json
{"verified": true}
```

Instead:

```yaml
verification_id: UUIDv7

subject:
  artifact:
    sha256: ...

claim:
  type: OUTPUT_SATISFIES_ACCEPTANCE_CONTRACT
  scope: final-output

verifier:
  id: research-quality-v3
  version: "3.1"
  method: inspect-ai

result:
  status: PASS | FAIL | INCONCLUSIVE
  score: "0.87"

evidence_refs:
  - ArtifactRef

limitations:
  - "Does not establish platform acceptance"
  - "Does not establish settlement"

issued_at: ...
```

This is where Inspect fits.

Inspect already supports arbitrary external agents, sandboxes, tasks and independent scoring, so it makes sense as a **certification/eval backend**, not as the WorkerKit execution engine. ([Inspect][6])

---

# Keep the Pāṭala epistemic ladder

Per claim:

```text
DECLARED
OBSERVED
DERIVED
VERIFIED
```

Example:

```text
"The worker used model X"
OBSERVED

"The output hash is ABC"
DERIVED

"The output passed verifier V"
VERIFIED

"The agent earned $20"
VERIFIED only when settlement evidence exists
```

This is substantially more useful than one global verification level.

---

# 10. `CommitDecision`

Every irreversible action passes one generic gate.

```yaml
commit_id: UUIDv7

run_id: ...

action:
  SUBMIT | PAY | PUBLISH | SIGN | DEPLOY | TRANSFER

target:
  adapter: taskmarket
  external_id: ...

subject:
  artifact:
    sha256: ...

checks:
  - id: artifact_matches_verified_subject
    status: PASS
    evidence_refs: [...]

  - id: acceptance_contract
    status: PASS

  - id: budget
    status: PASS

  - id: required_authority
    status: PASS

decision:
  ALLOW | DENY | REQUIRE_APPROVAL

policy_digest:
  sha256: ...

decided_at: ...
```

This generalizes both the Builda release gate and the Foxit/Proofdesk evidence gate.

It is one of the very few pieces of actual **control logic** WorkerKit should own.

---

# 11. Keep submission, outcome and settlement separate

Non-negotiable.

```text
SUBMITTED
≠
ACCEPTED
≠
PAID
```

