# `WorkReceipt` is not another bespoke crypto format

This is where I would simplify our previous thinking.

Use:

```text
in-toto Statement v1
    ↓
WorkerKit predicate
    ↓
DSSE
    ↓
Sigstore bundle
```

in-toto Statement v1 already defines:

```text
_type
subject[]
predicateType
predicate
```

and DSSE standardizes the signed envelope. ([Go Packages][5])

Sigstore bundles can carry the signature, certificate, timestamp and transparency-log material needed to verify later. ([Sigstore][8])

So:

```json
{
  "_type": "https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1",

  "subject": [
    {
      "name": "final-report.md",
      "digest": {
        "sha256": "..."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "worker-run-bundle",
      "digest": {
        "sha256": "..."
      }
    }
  ],

  "predicateType":
    "https://moltwork.com/attestation/worker-run/v1",

  "predicate": {
    "runId": "...",
    "workerManifestDigest": "...",
    "workOrderDigest": "...",

    "eventCheckpoint": {
      "root": "...",
      "firstSequence": 1,
      "lastSequence": 188
    },

    "economics": {
      "knownActualCost": "0.2381",
      "currency": "USD",
      "unpricedEvents": 0
    },

    "outputs": [...],

    "verificationRefs": [...],

    "submissionRef": "...",
    "outcomeRef": "...",
    "settlementRef": "..."
  }
}
```

That's enough.

Don't invent our own signing envelope.

