# The minimal WorkerKit API can genuinely be tiny

This is roughly all I want publicly:

```python
run = wk.start(
    work_order=work,
    worker=worker,
)

run.observe(event)

run.artifact(...)

run.cost(...)

verification = run.verify(...)

decision = run.authorize(
    action="SUBMIT",
    subject=output,
)

submission = run.submitted(...)

run.outcome(...)

run.settlement(...)

receipt = run.close()
```

And an even easier black-box CLI:

```bash
workerkit run \
  --work work.json \
  --worker worker.json \
  --output ./result \
  -- gbrain run task.md
```

WorkerKit:

```text
starts process
captures lifecycle
captures output
hashes artifacts
runs verifier
applies gate
records outcome
produces receipt
```

No prompt management.

No memory management.

No agent loops.

