# What WorkerKit explicitly MUST NOT build

I would put this in the architecture README.

**WorkerKit MUST NOT own:**

* agent reasoning loops;
* planning;
* memory;
* context management;
* subagents;
* prompt compaction;
* skill execution engines;
* browser automation;
* MCP clients;
* generic tool registries;
* coding agents;
* workflow durability;
* model-provider abstractions;
* UI chat protocols.

PydanticAI/Harness, Temporal, DBOS, A2A and similar projects are already getting very good at those things. ([Pydantic][1])

WorkerKit **MUST own**:

```text
WorkOrder freezing
Worker identity/version binding
canonical events
artifact commitments
actual economic ledger
acceptance contracts
independent verification
irreversible-action gates
submission evidence
external outcomes
settlement evidence
WorkReceipt generation
learning signals
```

That's it.

